### Sprint 5 — multi-user setup

### 1. Register admin (skip if already done in sprint1.http)
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@termchat.dev",
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "Password1!"
}

### 2. Register second user
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@termchat.dev",
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "Password1!"
}

### 3. Register third user
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@termchat.dev",
  "username": "bob",
  "password": "Password1!"
}

### 4. Login as admin — copy accessToken
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@termchat.dev",
  "password": "Password1!"
}

### 5. Create #general (admin token)
POST http://localhost:3000/channels
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "general",
  "description": "General discussion"
}

### 6. Create #random (admin token)
POST http://localhost:3000/channels
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "name": "random",
  "description": "Off-topic"
}

